IMPORT prelude
IMPORT tafdc

-- Cases for tafdc.l4. Expected values worked out by hand from the deposited 106 CMR 704.260, 704.270, 704.275, 704.280,
-- 704.281 and 704.500(A) and the posted Table of Need and Payment Standards, not copied from the encoding's output. The
-- family facts and the poverty limit are invented.

§ `Cases`

§§ `Need and Payment Standards (704.410, 704.420)`

#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 EQUALS 901
#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 3 FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS 861
#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 1 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 564
-- Size 12 with rent allowance: 1,925 + 2 x 153 = 2,231.
#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 12 TRUE FALSE 3 EQUALS 2231
-- Size 9 with rent allowance is $1,788, $50 above the no-rent figure where every other size is $40 above (finding 3).
#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 9 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS 1788
-- September 2026, size 3 with rent allowance, two children under 19: 901 + 2 x 500 = 1,901.
#ASSERT `What is my Need and Payment Standard` 3 TRUE TRUE 2 EQUALS 1901

§§ `Dependent care (704.275)`

-- 100 hours a month: the 88-130 row, $132 for a child of 2 or more and $150 under 2: cap 282; cost 400 gives 282, cost 200
-- gives 200. 160 hours: the full row, 175 + 200 = 375.
#ASSERT `How much dependent care can I deduct` 100 1 1 400 EQUALS 282
#ASSERT `How much dependent care can I deduct` 100 1 1 200 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `How much dependent care can I deduct` 160 1 1 400 EQUALS 375
#ASSERT `How much dependent care can I deduct` 40 2 0 400 EQUALS 88

§§ `The income test at application (704.260)`

-- Size 3, rent allowance: 901. Earnings $1,200, 160 hours, $300 for one child of 4 (capped at 175). No TAFDC in the last 4
-- months: 1,200 - 200 = 1,000, no 50% disregard, less 175 = 825; no other income: 825 <= 901, eligible.
#ASSERT `Does my family pass the TAFDC income test` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 1 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0
-- The same with $100 of child support: 925 > 901, not eligible.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does my family pass the TAFDC income test` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 1 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100))
-- TAFDC in the last 4 months: 1,000 x 50% = 500, less 175 = 325; with $500 unearned, 825 <= 901: eligible.
#ASSERT `Does my family pass the TAFDC income test` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 1 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 500
-- Left a better job without good cause: no $200, no 50%, no dependent care (704.270(B)(1), 704.275(B)(1)): 1,200 > 901.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does my family pass the TAFDC income test` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 1 0 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0))

§§ `The monthly grant (704.500(A))`

-- Size 3, rent allowance (901 both standards). Earnings $1,200, the six months of 100% disregard used: 1,200 - 200 = 1,000,
-- 50% = 500. Result 901 - 500 = 401: a grant of $401.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 6 1200 4000 0 0 EQUALS `answered` (`a monthly grant of` 401)
-- In the second month of a new job, household income 1,200 under 200% of poverty (4,000): 100% disregard; $300 of child
-- support only: 901 - 300 = 601.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 1500 4000 0 300 EQUALS `answered` (`a monthly grant of` 601)
-- Household income above 200% of poverty: no 100% disregard, so 500 counts as above, with the 300: 901 - 800 = 101.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 1200 160 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 4500 4000 0 300 EQUALS `answered` (`a monthly grant of` 101)
-- Unearned income $100.75 and nothing else: 901 - 100.75 = 800.25, rounded down to 800.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 4000 0 100.75 EQUALS `answered` (`a monthly grant of` 800)
-- Unearned income $895: result 6, under $10: receiving assistance but no grant.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 4000 0 895 EQUALS `answered` `receiving assistance, but no monthly grant, because the result is under $10`
-- Unearned income $950: result -49: financially ineligible.
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 4000 0 950 EQUALS `answered` `financially ineligible, because countable income exceeds the Need Standard`
-- No countable income at all: the result equals the Payment Standard, a case Step 7 does not state (finding 1).
#ASSERT `How much TAFDC will my family get` 3 TRUE FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 4000 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `Step 7 of 106 CMR 704.500(A) states no amount when the result equals the Payment Standard, which happens when the family has no countable income (NOTES.md finding 1)`

§§ `Reporting a change in deemed income (704.235(B)(1))`

#ASSERT EVALTRACE `704.235(B)(1) -- a change in deemed income must be reported within ten days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person whose income is deemed to the filing unit` `report the change in income to the Department` 7)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the person whose income is deemed -- nothing reported by day 11.
#TRACE `704.235(B)(1) -- a change in deemed income must be reported within ten days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
